      {
        "number": 3,
        "instructionsHtml": "Part 3<p>Listen and answer questions 21–30.</p>",
        "groups": [
          {
            "id": "part-3-group-1",
            "type": "mcq",
            "selectCount": 1,
            "rubricHtml": "<h3>Questions 21–26</h3><p>Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</p>",
            "questions": [
              {
                "number": 21,
                "textHtml": "Finn was pleased to discover that their topic",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "was not familiar to their module leader."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "had not been chosen by other students."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "did not prove to be difficult to research."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 22,
                "textHtml": "Maya says a mistaken belief about theatre programmes is that",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "theatres pay companies to produce them."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "few theatre-goers buy them nowadays."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "they contain far more adverts than previously."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 23,
                "textHtml": "Finn was surprised that, in early British theatre, programmes",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "were difficult for audiences to obtain."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "were given out free of charge."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "were seen as a kind of contract."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 24,
                "textHtml": "Maya feels their project should include an explanation of why companies of actors",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "promoted their own plays."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "performed plays outdoors."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "had to tour with their plays."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 25,
                "textHtml": "Finn and Maya both think that, compared to nineteenth-century programmes, those from the eighteenth century",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "were more original."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "were more colourful."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "were more informative."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "number": 26,
                "textHtml": "Maya doesn't fully understand why, in the twentieth century,",
                "options": [
                  {
                    "letter": "A",
                    "textHtml": "very few theatre programmes were printed in the USA."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "B",
                    "textHtml": "British theatre programmes failed to develop for so long."
                  },
                  {
                    "letter": "C",
                    "textHtml": "theatre programmes in Britain copied fashions from the USA."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
